    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d49">

                <pb facs="0120" n="100" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg100"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Benavides, minister
                        of foreign affairs, to Mr. Perry, United
                        States chargé d’affaires.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Madrid,
                                Palace</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1865-03-24"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 24,
                        1865</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that as soon
                    as I received your note of yesterday relative to the confederate steamer
                    Stonewall, I communicated it to the minister of marine, charging him that under
                    no pretext should he permit any work whatsoever to be done on said vessel. I
                    avail myself of this occasion to renew, &amp;c., &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. BENAVIDES.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chargé d’affaires</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">of the United States.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
